    "summaries": [
      {
        "action_date": "2026-02-04",
        "action_desc": "Reported to House",
        "text": "<p><strong>Weatherization Enhancement and Readiness Act of 2025</strong></p><p>This bill reauthorizes through FY2030 and modifies the Weatherization Assistance Program. Under the program, the Department of Energy (DOE) provides grants for low-income households to improve the energy efficiency of their homes.</p><p>The bill increases the cap on the average assistance provided per home from $6,500 to $12,000.</p><p>The bill also directs DOE to include in its annual report to Congress a description of the impacts of enhancement and innovation readiness efforts on eligibility for assistance under the program.</p>",
        "update_date": "2026-03-06T18:08:41Z"
      }
    ]
  },
